<!--Engine Documentation — RenderContext
  FQN: org.blockml.bml.engine.blockrender.documentation.RenderContext-->
<edoc:RenderContext xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:edoc="org.blockml.bml.engine.blockrender.documentation">

  <baseType>
    core:Documentation
  </baseType>
  <is>
    Per-block state passed into compile and callLLM
  </is>
  <documentation>
    RenderContext is internal. It is not part of the public compiler facade.
    compile and callLLM receive it. Template and copy methods identify files by
    path; they do not take a RenderContext in the V1 signature.

    Session fields (from CompileOptions):

        RenderSession
          typeRegistry
          sourceFilePath
          outputBasePath
          targetName
          documentKind
          activeConfig     optional
          mbLibPath        optional — domain library root for relative imports

    Per-node fields:

        RenderContext
          session
          blockFqn
          outputRelativePath
          parentPartId     optional
          partId           optional
          instance         optional
          withScope        readonly map of bml:with bindings
          loopScope        optional readonly map
          activePresetId   optional
          child(overrides) forked context without replacing session

    Composition rendering forks context via child(). Property values are resolved
    on demand by the processor (PropertyResolver). V1 does not cache them on the
    context.

    Canonical BOM stays immutable. expandDirectives and auto-ids, when a processor
    needs them, run on a working copy before compile. The engine does not write
    those ids back to the BomDocument.

  </documentation>
  <references>
    <see type="edoc:RenderOutput" relation="ReadNext" />
  </references>
</edoc:RenderContext>
